<title>CANADA: CANADA'S PRAIRIES TO SEE RAIN IN WEST, SUN IN EAST.</title>
<headline>CANADA'S PRAIRIES TO SEE RAIN IN WEST, SUN IN EAST.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Tuesday were forecast to see rain in the west and sun in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see afternoon scattered showers and highs of 22 to 25 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see sunny skies and highs of 20 to 24 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see mainly sunny skies with highs of 18 to 20 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
